## 5. Scope audit

- Every structural step is inherited from the independently hostile-audited `0.0021`
  theorem. This note changes only the certified scalar endpoint and downstream
  arithmetic.
- The new atomic verifier derives its `sqrt(Delta_2)` bracket from outward rational
  bounds on `pi` and `sqrt(3)`.
- The interval mesh enlarges the actual center-imbalance domain and rounds every loss
  term upward.
- The Section-171 verifier uses a strict endpoint-negativity margin greater than
  `3e-5`, not a floating-point root.
- The rhombic-only transfer inherits exactly the scope passed by the `0.0021` hostile
  audit.
- Low-`t`, bridge-subtracted, detour-free, and singleton-leaf consequences are only
  algebraic propagations; their original geometric hypotheses remain binding.
- Contact-isolated points remain in the full source.
- No exact unit equilateral triangle or strict same-cardinality sub-`D` source is
  produced.

**Disposition:** new strongest proof-only scalar endpoint, awaiting independent audit.
C-II and Level I remain open.
